BBUUGGSS
     The functions ggeettggrreenntt(), ggeettggrrnnaamm(), ggeettggrrggiidd(), sseettggrroouuppeenntt() and
     sseettggrreenntt() leave their results in an internal static object and return a
     pointer to that object.  Subsequent calls to the same function will mod‐
     ify the same object.

     The functions ggeettggrreenntt(), ggeettggrreenntt__rr(), eennddggrreenntt(), sseettggrroouuppeenntt(), and
     sseettggrreenntt() are fairly useless in a networked environment and should be
     avoided, if possible.  The ggeettggrreenntt() and ggeettggrreenntt__rr() functions make no
     attempt to suppress duplicate information if multiple sources are speci‐
     fied in nsswitch.conf(5).

